<title>LITHUANIA: BALTIJOS SHARE ISSUE REGISTERED.</title>
<headline>BALTIJOS SHARE ISSUE REGISTERED.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's securities commission said on Monday it has registered the 34.59 million litas share capital boost of Baltijos Shipyard, in which Danish Odense owns a 40 percent stake.</p>
<p>The securities commission said in a statement that the new issue raises the capital of the company to 69.18 million litas.</p>
<p>The state owns 32.5 percent of Baltijos Shipyard and it has said that it take up its portion of the new share issue.</p>
<p>But the government has also decided to privatise its shares in the company this year.</p>
<p>The Danish Odense company bought at more than 40 percent of the company last month for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
